Final external-contract decision for Lantern customer preview v0 (2024-05-15)

Iris and Alex reviewed an export of the internal Lantern read model against the publication guidance. The internal shape is not an approved customer export format and must not be reused directly.

Approved external projection:
- Deploy events are published as provenance-backed, service-facing events (including the deploy transition and observation time), rather than exposing internal record fields.
- Service ownership is published only as an external service-facing label with its verification timestamp and safe provenance. Ownership inferred from room context is excluded; absent or unverified ownership is represented explicitly as unknown.
- Incident load is published only as a service-scoped summary with its source/observation timestamp. Missing source data is represented explicitly as unknown.
- Customer-safe provenance explains the source and Lantern transformation using the approved safe fields (including source system/reference, collection or observation time, transform version, and emitting adapter) without exposing internal identifiers or raw internal records. Source links are permitted only where the viewer is authorized to access the source.

Explicit exclusions:
- raw incident text;
- internal room names or other internal room metadata;
- individual comparisons;
- ownership inferred from room context;
- employee IDs;
- internal permission identifiers;
- internal owner-map record IDs;
- any fallback to internal-only fields or direct pass-through of internal provenance identifiers.

Implementation guardrail: the external preview contract must be a separate explicit projection/adapter. Do not silently map, reuse, or fall back to the internal read-model shape when an external field is absent. No customer access is granted by this decision.

